# Exceptions for scripts/check-comments.py: "<path glob> :: <regex>" or "<path glob> :: <kind> ::
# <regex>" (kind = dead path | notes pointer | provenance/status | version | long comment), matched
# against the comment line (a long comment's first line that is not a rule). Add one only when the
# number or path IS the mechanism (a threshold the code tests, a dependency floor, a foreign tree
# path), the wording is a licence attribution, every line of a long comment is its own trap, or the
# text is not a comment at all (printed heredoc), never for a ledger fact. Each line names specific
# comments: a catch-all regex, a line matching nothing or more than 6 lines, or a long-comment line
# on a glob or covering two blocks in one file fails.
kernel/*/kernel.conf :: ROCKNIX's
scripts/lib.sh :: common-skip
packages/shared/pocknix-steam/pocknix-game-launch :: c000007b
packages/shared/pocknix-tools/pocknix-internal-boot-rename :: from ROCKNIX to POCKNIX
packages/shared/pocknix-sdcard-automount/format-device.sh :: SteamOS's deck
scripts/build-kernel.sh :: long comment :: ^# Deltas over the synced config
packages/shared/pocknix-tools/pocknix-install-internal :: long comment :: ^#\$UD_NUM  userdata
# #135 edits a line of this block: cut it to the bar once #135 lands.
config/pocknix.conf :: long comment :: ^# Image target
